  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the meme creator (the man)",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the man in the plaid shirt, who is visually and textually represented as the 'me' in the meme. The text explicitly uses 'me' ('i don't need you to tell me...') and 'my memes', directly identifying the man as the speaker and the subject of the frustration. The user sees themselves as the meme creator being reported, and the visual of the man pointing aggressively embodies this self-referential projection. The user is projecting their own experience of being reported onto this visual and textual representation.",
